<PageLayout title="Accessibility information"><main id="main" class="legal-main"><p class="eyebrow">ACCESSIBILITY INFORMATION</p><h1>Built to be<br/>easy to use.</h1><p><Wordmark inline/> includes keyboard navigation, visible focus indicators, labeled form fields, responsive pages, and a skip-to-content link.</p><h2>Motion controls</h2><p>The footer has a “Pause ambience” control. The site also respects your device’s reduced-motion preference. The background is decorative and is not needed to understand any page.</p><h2>Forms and sample websites</h2><p>Forms identify required fields and show a reviewable draft before you choose to email or download it. The fictional sample websites include keyboard-operable controls and clearly labeled preview behavior.</p><h2>Ongoing review</h2><p>I’m continuing to review the site’s accessibility. If a page or control makes it difficult to use, please tell me so I can look into it.</p><h2>Report a difficulty</h2><p><a href="mailto:tkjet718@gmail.com?subject=TemVora%20accessibility%20feedback">Email me with accessibility feedback</a>. If you can, describe the page, your browser or assistive technology, and the action you were trying to take.</p></main></PageLayout>